/* book: lead: A psychrometric chart, also called a humidity chart, puts every property of moist air on one sheet. Dry-bulb temperature runs along the bottom and humidity up the side. Any two independent readings fix a point, and the rest — dew point, relative humidity, wet-bulb temperature, enthalpy, humid volume — are read from lines through that point. It exists to save repeated calculations in drying, coolin */
